        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {
            "urls": [
              {
                "display_url": "intangible.ai",
                "end": 1934,
                "expanded_url": "http://intangible.ai",
                "start": 1911,
                "url": "https://t.co/sWmUrq5ba3"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Intangible just launched 2.0 today, one AI studio for image, video and 3D.\n\nCEO Bharat Vasan announced it on X on Nov 11, 2026. His launch post pitches it as a way to get the idea in your head onto a screen, for filmmakers and founders alike. To prove it, he put cofounder Charles Migos in his own action sequence, 100% shot in Intangible. The video runs 1:54 and the post passed 118K views.\n\nThe headline feature is Canvas. It's one board that holds your brief, your references, a real 3D scene and the renders that come out of it. You describe a project and bring your files, then Intangible's agents plan it, build one 3D scene and render from it.\n\nThe point is control. Most AI video tools generate a shot, and if you want a different camera angle or a moved object, you often start over. Here a real 3D world sits under the AI. You can place objects and lighting, position cameras, change objects and generate many shots from the same scene without re-prompting each one. You can also revisit the brief and talk through changes in chat.\n\nCreators who tried it showed what that looks like. Heather Cooper made an action teaser for her series idea The Rider. Umesh planned camera angles in 3D for a Mars landing scene before generating the shots. JACKJ used one scene for a full clothing collection and the individual product shots. Companies like JetZero are already using it.\n\nReactions focused on the workflow. Bilawal Sidhu said a spatial 3D reference makes iterating much faster, and you no longer need Blender or another 3D tool. Ex-Unity exec Troy Kirwin called it the dream from his Unity days. Investor Nate Williams praised the team's momentum. Many of the launch-day demos were labeled paid partnerships.\n\nKey numbers:\n- Launch date: Nov 11, 2026\n- Free plan: $0, with 150 free credits\n- Explorer plan: $25 billed annually, listed down from $35\n- Launch video: 1:54\n\nIntangible 2.0 is live now at https://t.co/sWmUrq5ba3."
        },
